owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ShinryakuTako/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T23:01:18Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T23:01:18Z","body":"Is this what caused all the bloat in `.import` files??\r\n\r\n```\r\nprocess/channel_remap/red=0\r\nprocess/channel_remap/green=1\r\nprocess/channel_remap/blue=2\r\nprocess/channel_remap/alpha=3\r\n```\r\n\r\nCan this clutter be avoided by not explicitly writing out obvious defaults? All of a sudden I have 69 changes to commit… 😓","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050507434/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050529291","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99676#issuecomment-3050529291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99676","id":3050529291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6102IL","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T23:11:57Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T23:11:57Z","body":"> Is this what caused all the bloat in `.import` files??\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> process/channel_remap/red=0\r\n> process/channel_remap/green=1\r\n> process/channel_remap/blue=2\r\n> process/channel_remap/alpha=3\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Can this clutter be avoided by not explicitly writing out obvious defaults? All of a sudden I have 69 changes to commit… 😓\r\n\r\nI’m usually not a fan of having implicit defaults… but this is one scenario where I think using default is extremely valid, if it’s both possible and reasonable to implement it this way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3050529291/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059335462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99676#issuecomment-3059335462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99676","id":3059335462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62WcEm","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T22:29:56Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T22:31:49Z","body":"`.import` files and export presets always write default values, while PackedScene and ProjectSettings never do.\r\n\r\nIt's technically feasible to add a property usage flag to override this behavior on a per-property basis, but it has some ramifications. It means we no longer have this guarantee that we can safely change a value across minor Godot versions and not have it change on every existing resource out there. We took advantage of this on `.import` files and export presets multiple times throughout the 4.x cycle so far :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3059335462/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4760630011","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99676#issuecomment-4760630011","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99676","id":4760630011,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG8Fy-w","user":{"login":"FyiurAmron","id":11016998,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDE2OTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11016998?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron","html_url":"https://github.com/FyiurAmron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-21T02:08:58Z","updated_at":"2026-06-21T02:40:22Z","body":"@BlueCube3310 a good question that came to me due to @allenwp 's question: how is it that `1.0 - src` is working fine when source data is sRGB-encoded? For other remaps sRGB is not a problem, but I couldn't find any forced linearization in the import code for this case, and obviously `1.0 - src` for sRGB data should produce very different results than for linear, yet testing in the editor showed the expected output after inv, so I guess the linearization does happen somewhere else before going into remapping?? Couldn't find it though, and enabling forced linearization actually _breaks_ the inversion?\r\n\r\nI've spent a couple of hours trying to get my head around this, but I'm none the wiser BTW :)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4760630011/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4769569283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99676#issuecomment-4769569283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99676","id":4769569283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHEnaAw","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T14:48:34Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T14:48:34Z","body":"> how is it that `1.0 - src` is working fine when source data is sRGB-encoded?\r\n\r\nThis is generally the desired behaviour: if you have a value that is around 50% brightness, the user expects the inverse to also be around 50% brightness, which is the result that you get when performing this inverse math on nonlinear sRGB-encoded values. If the value uses linear encoding, this would be something like a change from 0.2 to 0.8, so it would go from 50% brightness to a higher brightness.\r\n\r\nI believe this means that this inverse remap option doesn’t work well for linear-encoded formats like EXR, but these are typically HDR formats where the math simply won’t ever work because the format stores values above 1.0.\r\n\r\nSo this behaviour is reasonable and intended.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4769569283/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]